{"title":"Career Roadmap: Forensic Assistant","role":"Forensic Assistant","summary":"A Forensic Assistant supports forensic professionals, investigating agencies, laboratories or crime-scene teams with activities such as:","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts - General / Honours)","Course":"Criminology & Police Administration"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Build foundations in criminology, criminal justice, evidence handling, forensic procedures, documentation, investigation and basic scientific/technical awareness"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Forensic Assistant supports forensic professionals, investigating agencies, laboratories or crime-scene teams with activities such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Evidence documentation"},{"text":"Evidence collection support"},{"text":"Scene documentation"},{"text":"Evidence packaging and labelling"},{"text":"Chain-of-custody records"},{"text":"Photography/documentation"},{"text":"Case-file organization"},{"text":"Laboratory administrative support"},{"text":"Sample tracking"},{"text":"Digital record management"},{"text":"Coordination with investigating officers and forensic experts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important qualification distinction"},{"type":"p","text":"A BA in Criminology & Police Administration is relevant to the criminal-justice and investigative side of forensic support, but it does not automatically qualify a graduate for scientific forensic analyst roles involving DNA analysis, toxicology, forensic chemistry, biology or advanced laboratory examination."},{"type":"p","text":"Those roles commonly require specialized Forensic Science, Biology, Chemistry, Biotechnology or related scientific qualifications, depending on the employer and jurisdiction."},{"type":"p","text":"Therefore, this BA pathway should primarily target forensic support, evidence/documentation, investigation-support and criminal-justice roles, unless the student obtains additional science/forensic qualifications."},{"type":"p","text":"A practical pathway is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Criminology & Police Administration","Criminal Justice","Investigation","Evidence Handling","Forensic Fundamentals","Crime-Scene Documentation","Chain of Custody","Internship","Forensic/Investigation Support Role","Specialized Training/PG where required"]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof of Skill","Gap to Avoid"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Criminal-justice foundation"},{"text":"Criminology, criminal law, policing"},{"text":"Case-study portfolio"},{"text":"Learning only theory"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Investigation & evidence"},{"text":"Police administration, investigation, forensic fundamentals"},{"text":"Mock investigation"},{"text":"Poor evidence documentation"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Forensic support skills"},{"text":"Crime-scene procedures, documentation, digital records"},{"text":"Forensic case portfolio"},{"text":"Treating forensic work as only laboratory science"}],[{"text":"Year 4*"},{"text":"Practical specialization"},{"text":"Internship, evidence management, advanced forensic support"},{"text":"Supervised internship + capstone"},{"text":"No field/lab exposure"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"*For a 4-year honours structure. In a 3-year BA, integrate the final-stage objectives into the third year."}]},{"heading":"Semester-by-Semester Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Semester 1 — Criminology Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Introduction to criminology"},{"text":"Crime and deviance"},{"text":"Criminal behaviour"},{"text":"Victimology"},{"text":"Sociology"},{"text":"Psychology fundamentals"},{"text":"Indian criminal-justice system"},{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Academic writing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Crime","Victim","Investigation","Evidence","Prosecution","Trial","Justice"]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 2 — Criminal Justice & Police Administration"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Police organization"},{"text":"Investigation process"},{"text":"Criminal courts"},{"text":"Prosecution"},{"text":"Corrections"},{"text":"Prison administration"},{"text":"Juvenile justice"},{"text":"Community policing"},{"text":"Criminal justice institutions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the roles of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Police"},{"text":"Investigators"},{"text":"Prosecutors"},{"text":"Courts"},{"text":"Forensic experts"},{"text":"Correctional institutions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 3 — Criminal Investigation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the investigation lifecycle:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Complaint/Information","Initial Response","Scene Protection","Evidence Identification","Documentation","Collection","Packaging","Examination","Analysis","Reporting","Court"]},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Crime-scene management"},{"text":"Investigative interviewing"},{"text":"Witness handling"},{"text":"Evidence identification"},{"text":"Case documentation"},{"text":"Investigation planning"},{"text":"Crime reconstruction fundamentals"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the distinction between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Evidence collection","Forensic examination","Interpretation","Expert opinion"]},{"type":"p","text":"A support professional should not represent themselves as the scientific expert unless appropriately qualified."},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 4 — Forensic Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop basic awareness of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Physical Evidence"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Biological evidence"},{"text":"Hair"},{"text":"Fibres"},{"text":"Glass"},{"text":"Soil"},{"text":"Paint"},{"text":"Firearms-related evidence"},{"text":"Tool marks"},{"text":"Documents"},{"text":"Trace evidence"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Biological Evidence"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand at a high level:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Blood"},{"text":"Saliva"},{"text":"Hair"},{"text":"Tissue"},{"text":"DNA"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Chemical Evidence"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the role of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Toxicology"},{"text":"Drugs"},{"text":"Poisons"},{"text":"Alcohol"},{"text":"Chemical residues"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The BA student should understand what different forensic disciplines do, even when laboratory analysis requires specialist science qualifications."}]},{"heading":"Crime-Scene Management","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn the principles of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Scene security"},{"text":"Scene preservation"},{"text":"Entry/exit documentation"},{"text":"Evidence identification"},{"text":"Photography"},{"text":"Sketching"},{"text":"Notes"},{"text":"Evidence numbering"},{"text":"Packaging"},{"text":"Labelling"},{"text":"Documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Basic workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Secure","Observe","Document","Photograph","Map/Sketch","Identify","Collect","Package","Label","Record","Transfer"]},{"type":"p","text":"Avoid unnecessary handling or movement of evidence."}]},{"heading":"Evidence Documentation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A forensic assistant should be extremely precise."},{"type":"p","text":"Record:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case number"},{"text":"Evidence number"},{"text":"Description"},{"text":"Location found"},{"text":"Date/time"},{"text":"Collector"},{"text":"Packaging"},{"text":"Transfer information"},{"text":"Storage information"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"h","text":"Chain of Custody"},{"type":"p","text":"The chain of custody establishes:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Who had the evidence","When","Where","Why","How it was transferred"]},{"type":"p","text":"Breaks or inconsistencies in documentation can undermine evidentiary reliability."}]},{"heading":"Evidence Packaging & Preservation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn the principles of appropriate packaging for different evidence categories."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Contamination prevention"},{"text":"Cross-contamination"},{"text":"Moisture concerns"},{"text":"Labelling"},{"text":"Sealing"},{"text":"Tamper-evident handling"},{"text":"Storage conditions"},{"text":"Transportation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Exact procedures vary by evidence type and agency protocol, so students should follow current laboratory/agency SOPs rather than relying solely on classroom rules."}]},{"heading":"Forensic Photography & Documentation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn basic:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Crime-scene photography"},{"text":"Overall photographs"},{"text":"Mid-range photographs"},{"text":"Close-up photographs"},{"text":"Scale photography"},{"text":"Evidence photography"},{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"Image metadata"},{"text":"File organization"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Also develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Scene sketches"},{"text":"Measurements"},{"text":"Evidence maps"},{"text":"Written observations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The objective is to create a reproducible record of the scene."}]},{"heading":"Fingerprint & Impression Evidence — Awareness","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Study the fundamentals of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fingerprint patterns"},{"text":"Latent prints"},{"text":"Patent prints"},{"text":"Plastic impressions"},{"text":"Footwear impressions"},{"text":"Tire impressions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand at a conceptual level:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Detection","Documentation","Recovery","Comparison","Interpretation"]},{"type":"p","text":"Specialized evidence processing should be performed only with appropriate training, equipment and authorization."}]},{"heading":"Questioned Documents","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop basic awareness of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Handwriting"},{"text":"Signatures"},{"text":"Alterations"},{"text":"Erasures"},{"text":"Printing"},{"text":"Ink"},{"text":"Paper"},{"text":"Document authenticity"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the difference between:"},{"type":"p","text":"Document collection/documentation and expert forensic document examination."}]},{"heading":"Digital Forensics Awareness","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A modern forensic-support professional should understand the digital evidence lifecycle."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn conceptually:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital evidence"},{"text":"Computers"},{"text":"Mobile devices"},{"text":"Cloud data"},{"text":"Metadata"},{"text":"Logs"},{"text":"CCTV"},{"text":"Digital photographs"},{"text":"Email"},{"text":"Social-media evidence"},{"text":"File systems"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Basic workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Identify","Preserve","Acquire","Examine","Analyze","Document","Report"]},{"type":"p","text":"Actual digital forensic acquisition and examination requires specialized tools, training and authorization."}]},{"heading":"Cybercrime Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cybercrime types"},{"text":"Online fraud"},{"text":"Identity theft"},{"text":"Account compromise"},{"text":"Cyberstalking"},{"text":"Digital evidence"},{"text":"Online investigation concepts"},{"text":"Cybersecurity fundamentals"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"IP addresses"},{"text":"Logs"},{"text":"Metadata"},{"text":"Timestamps"},{"text":"Authentication records"},{"text":"Digital footprints"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Do not confuse cyber-forensics support with offensive cybersecurity or unauthorized access."}]},{"heading":"Forensic Psychology & Behaviour","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminal behaviour"},{"text":"Victim behaviour"},{"text":"Interview psychology"},{"text":"Eyewitness memory"},{"text":"Cognitive biases"},{"text":"Trauma awareness"},{"text":"Behavioural patterns"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand limitations of behavioural profiling."},{"type":"p","text":"Avoid treating behavioural indicators as definitive proof of guilt or innocence."}]},{"heading":"Forensic Toxicology & Biology Awareness","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The BA pathway should understand the role of specialist disciplines."},{"type":"h","text":"Forensic Biology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"DNA"},{"text":"Blood"},{"text":"Body fluids"},{"text":"Biological traces"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Toxicology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Drugs"},{"text":"Poisons"},{"text":"Alcohol"},{"text":"Toxic substances"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Forensic Chemistry"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unknown substances"},{"text":"Chemical residues"},{"text":"Material analysis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"These are primarily laboratory-science domains and generally require relevant scientific qualifications for analyst-level work."}]},{"heading":"Forensic Databases & Documentation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn to manage:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case numbers"},{"text":"Evidence inventories"},{"text":"Laboratory submissions"},{"text":"Reports"},{"text":"Photographs"},{"text":"Chain-of-custody records"},{"text":"Case status"},{"text":"Court documentation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful tools:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Google Sheets"},{"text":"Database fundamentals"},{"text":"Document management systems"},{"text":"Case-management software"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Excel skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"XLOOKUP"},{"text":"INDEX/MATCH"},{"text":"IF"},{"text":"COUNTIFS"},{"text":"SUMIFS"},{"text":"PivotTables"},{"text":"Data validation"},{"text":"Conditional formatting"},{"text":"Filters"},{"text":"Charts"}]}]},{"heading":"Research & Crime Analysis","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Crime statistics"},{"text":"Crime mapping"},{"text":"Crime trends"},{"text":"Victimization studies"},{"text":"Geographic patterns"},{"text":"Recidivism"},{"text":"Criminal-justice datasets"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful tools:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"GIS/QGIS"},{"text":"Basic statistics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential analyses:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Crime by location"},{"text":"Crime by time"},{"text":"Crime type"},{"text":"Victim demographics"},{"text":"Case clearance"},{"text":"Recurrence patterns"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Correlation should not automatically be interpreted as causation."}]},{"heading":"Legal & Ethical Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminal law fundamentals"},{"text":"Criminal procedure"},{"text":"Evidence principles"},{"text":"Constitutional rights"},{"text":"Privacy"},{"text":"Search and seizure concepts"},{"text":"Due process"},{"text":"Witness rights"},{"text":"Victim rights"},{"text":"Chain of custody"},{"text":"Expert evidence"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Also study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Confidentiality"},{"text":"Impartiality"},{"text":"Evidence integrity"},{"text":"Documentation accuracy"},{"text":"Conflict of interest"},{"text":"Professional ethics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A forensic professional's role is to document and interpret evidence objectively, not to prove a predetermined theory."}]},{"heading":"Projects to Build","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Mock Crime-Scene Documentation"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a fictional scene using safe, non-hazardous props."},{"type":"p","text":"Produce:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Scene photographs"},{"text":"Scene sketch"},{"text":"Evidence numbering"},{"text":"Evidence inventory"},{"text":"Chain-of-custody form"},{"text":"Scene report"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Do not use real crime scenes or sensitive personal information."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Crime Data Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Use a public or synthetic dataset."},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Crime type"},{"text":"Geography"},{"text":"Time"},{"text":"Trends"},{"text":"Victim categories"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel analysis"},{"text":"Power BI dashboard"},{"text":"GIS map"},{"text":"Short analytical report"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Evidence Management System"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a simulated system for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case registration"},{"text":"Evidence inventory"},{"text":"Evidence location"},{"text":"Chain of custody"},{"text":"Laboratory submission"},{"text":"Report status"},{"text":"Case closure"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use only synthetic data."}]},{"heading":"Advanced Capstone Project","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Forensic Evidence & Criminal Investigation Support Platform"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a simulated case-management system containing:"},{"type":"h","text":"Case Management"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case ID"},{"text":"Incident details"},{"text":"Investigation status"},{"text":"Assigned personnel"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Evidence Management"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Evidence ID"},{"text":"Description"},{"text":"Location"},{"text":"Collection information"},{"text":"Packaging"},{"text":"Chain of custody"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Scene Documentation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Photographs"},{"text":"Sketches"},{"text":"Evidence map"},{"text":"Investigator notes"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Forensic Coordination"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Laboratory submission"},{"text":"Examination type"},{"text":"Status"},{"text":"Report tracking"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Analytics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case trends"},{"text":"Evidence status"},{"text":"Processing time"},{"text":"Crime categories"},{"text":"Geographic patterns"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final deliverables"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case file"},{"text":"Evidence register"},{"text":"Chain-of-custody documentation"},{"text":"Scene report"},{"text":"Investigation workflow"},{"text":"Dashboard"},{"text":"Final analytical report"}]}]},{"heading":"Technology Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Essential"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Word"},{"text":"PowerPoint"},{"text":"Digital documentation"},{"text":"Database fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Useful"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"QGIS"},{"text":"Digital evidence-management systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted document analysis"},{"text":"Computer vision"},{"text":"Digital evidence triage"},{"text":"Automated pattern analysis"},{"text":"Crime analytics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"AI-generated results should be treated as assistance requiring human validation, especially when evidence may affect legal proceedings."}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Forensic laboratories"},{"text":"Police departments"},{"text":"Crime-investigation units"},{"text":"Criminal-justice organizations"},{"text":"Legal-support organizations"},{"text":"Correctional institutions"},{"text":"Cybercrime units"},{"text":"Security organizations"},{"text":"Research institutions"},{"text":"Universities with forensic programmes"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For this BA pathway, particularly valuable exposure includes:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Evidence documentation"},{"text":"Case-file management"},{"text":"Crime-scene observation"},{"text":"Investigation support"},{"text":"Crime analysis"},{"text":"Laboratory administration"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Actual laboratory examination should only be performed under appropriate supervision and authorization."}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful supplementary areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Forensic fundamentals"},{"text":"Crime-scene investigation"},{"text":"Evidence management"},{"text":"Criminal investigation"},{"text":"Fingerprint fundamentals"},{"text":"Forensic photography"},{"text":"Cybercrime awareness"},{"text":"Digital forensics fundamentals"},{"text":"Crime analysis"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Criminal justice"},{"text":"Data analytics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Certifications should not be presented as substitutes for the formal scientific qualifications required for specialist forensic laboratory roles."}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Careers","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Realistic roles include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Forensic Assistant"},{"text":"Forensic Support Assistant"},{"text":"Crime-Scene Support Assistant"},{"text":"Evidence Management Assistant"},{"text":"Investigation Assistant"},{"text":"Criminal Justice Assistant"},{"text":"Case Documentation Assistant"},{"text":"Forensic Laboratory Support Assistant"},{"text":"Crime Analysis Assistant"},{"text":"Police Administration Assistant"},{"text":"Investigation Support Associate"},{"text":"Digital Evidence Support Assistant"},{"text":"Research Assistant — Criminology"},{"text":"Criminal Justice Research Associate"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For laboratory analyst roles involving scientific examination, additional qualifications may be required."}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Forensic Science"},{"type":"p","text":"For students wanting deeper forensic specialization:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MSc Forensic Science"},{"text":"MSc Forensic Science & Criminology"},{"text":"PG Diploma in Forensic Science"},{"text":"Specialized forensic programmes"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Eligibility must be checked carefully because many forensic-science programmes require a science/biology/chemistry-related undergraduate background."},{"type":"h","text":"Criminology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MA Criminology"},{"text":"MA Criminology & Criminal Justice"},{"text":"Criminal Justice"},{"text":"Police Administration"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cybercrime"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cybercrime"},{"text":"Cyber Forensics"},{"text":"Cybersecurity"},{"text":"Digital Forensics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Again, programme eligibility varies."},{"type":"h","text":"Public Administration"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MA Public Administration"},{"text":"Public Policy"},{"text":"Governance"}]}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Potential postgraduate fields:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MSc Forensic Science"},{"text":"MSc Forensic Investigation"},{"text":"MSc Crime Scene Investigation"},{"text":"MSc Criminology"},{"text":"Criminal Justice"},{"text":"Digital Forensics"},{"text":"Cybercrime"},{"text":"Forensic Psychology"},{"text":"Security Studies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Before applying, verify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Undergraduate subject prerequisites"},{"text":"Laboratory requirements"},{"text":"Professional accreditation"},{"text":"Practicum"},{"text":"Background checks"},{"text":"Employment eligibility"},{"text":"Professional recognition"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A forensic qualification from another country does not automatically establish eligibility for every forensic role in India."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Forensic Support"},{"type":"h","text":"Forensic Assistant"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Forensic/Investigation Assistant"},{"type":"h","text":"Forensic Support Officer / Evidence Coordinator"},{"type":"h","text":"Forensic Operations Coordinator"},{"type":"h","text":"Forensic/Investigation Support Manager"},{"type":"h","text":"Investigation Route"},{"type":"h","text":"Investigation Assistant"},{"type":"h","text":"Investigation Officer/Analyst"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Investigation Analyst"},{"type":"h","text":"Investigation/Crime Analysis Lead"},{"type":"h","text":"Scientific Forensics Route"},{"type":"p","text":"For those who obtain the required science/forensic qualifications:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Forensic Laboratory Trainee","Forensic Analyst","Senior Analyst","Technical/Scientific Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"Titles and eligibility vary by organization."}]},{"heading":"Long-Term Relevance: 2030–2046","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Forensic and criminal-justice work will increasingly involve:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital evidence"},{"text":"Cybercrime"},{"text":"AI-assisted evidence analysis"},{"text":"Computer vision"},{"text":"Geographic crime analytics"},{"text":"Digital chain of custody"},{"text":"Automated evidence management"},{"text":"CCTV analytics"},{"text":"Biometrics"},{"text":"Forensic databases"},{"text":"Data-driven policing"},{"text":"Privacy-preserving investigation technologies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest future support profile is likely to combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Criminology","Evidence Management","Investigation","Digital Forensics Awareness","Data Analytics","Ethics"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Criminal Justice"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminology"},{"text":"Criminal law fundamentals"},{"text":"Criminal procedure"},{"text":"Police administration"},{"text":"Investigation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Forensic Support"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Evidence identification"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Photography"},{"text":"Packaging principles"},{"text":"Chain of custody"},{"text":"Crime-scene management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Scientific Awareness"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Biology"},{"text":"DNA"},{"text":"Toxicology"},{"text":"Chemistry"},{"text":"Trace evidence"},{"text":"Fingerprints"},{"text":"Questioned documents"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital evidence"},{"text":"Cybercrime"},{"text":"Metadata"},{"text":"Digital documentation"},{"text":"Evidence-management systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Analytics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"GIS"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Report writing"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Attention to detail"},{"text":"Evidence integrity"},{"text":"Confidentiality"},{"text":"Ethical reasoning"}]}]},{"heading":"Final Portfolio Target","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should ideally have:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strong criminology foundation"},{"text":"Criminal-justice knowledge"},{"text":"Police-administration understanding"},{"text":"Crime-scene documentation project"},{"text":"Evidence-management project"},{"text":"Chain-of-custody simulation"},{"text":"Forensic photography portfolio"},{"text":"Crime-data analysis"},{"text":"Power BI crime-analysis dashboard"},{"text":"Basic GIS crime map"},{"text":"Digital-forensics awareness project"},{"text":"Forensic case-study portfolio"},{"text":"Investigation-support internship"},{"text":"Evidence-handling/safeguarding training"},{"text":"Clear postgraduate specialization plan"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target Graduate Profile"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Criminology & Police Administration","Criminology","Criminal Justice","Police Administration","Investigation","Evidence Management","Crime-Scene Documentation","Chain of Custody","Forensic Fundamentals","Digital Evidence Awareness","Crime Analysis","Excel/Power BI/GIS","Internship","Forensic/Investigation Support Assistant","Senior Support/Investigation Role","Specialized Forensic/Criminal-Justice Qualification","Forensic Support Leadership / Investigation / Crime Analysis"]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"If the student's ultimate goal is to become a DNA analyst, forensic biologist, forensic chemist, toxicologist or other laboratory-based forensic scientist, this BA route should generally be reconsidered in favor of an appropriate science/forensic-science degree pathway."},{"type":"table","header":["ID","Level","Stream","Degree","Course","Career","Notes"],"rows":[[{"text":"1474"},{"text":"UG"},{"text":"Humanities & Social Sciences"},{"text":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)"},{"text":"Criminology & Police Administration"},{"text":"Corrections Officer"},{"text":"—"}]]}]}]}